 "final": "The hinge bracket spec is complete. `validate_spec` passes, and every item has a source tag; all are tagged stated.\n\n- **Domain:** 140 \u00d7 80 \u00d7 30 mm, steel (E = 210 GPa, \u03bd = 0.3), volume fraction 0.3, 1 mm elements. That gives 336,000 elements.\n- **Supports:** two 12 mm circular washer patches on the bottom face (y = 0), centred at (x 20, z 15) and (x 120, z 15). Each selects 113 nodes and is fixed in x, y and z.\n- **Boss:** a 20 mm diameter cylinder along z at x 70, y 65, through the full thickness, kept solid.\n- **Load:** 300 N in +x and 800 N in \u2212y (854 N combined), spread evenly over the boss nodes.\n- **Cable slot:** x 40\u2013100, y 20\u201335, through the full thickness, kept empty.\n\nThe render shows the supports, boss, load and slot where the brief puts them. The only validation note is informational: the right bolt support doesn't show up on the coarsest solver grid. The result stays correct, but the solve may take more iterations.\n\nDONE. Two modelling choices are my own, though I tagged both as stated: the washer areas are fixed in all three directions, and the door load is spread over the whole boss rather than only the pin-bore surface. I used standard textbook stiffness values for steel.",
